Session 32 summary — the zero_silent_loss root cause is found and the fix is built, pending verification:

**Root cause (proven):** every dir coherency fence (`mxfs_dir_evict_data_blocks`, `mxfs_dir_drain_evict_data_blocks`) silently bailed when the shared storm dir grew into **BTREE format** — and the eager evict returned `true` ("all evicted"), a lie that advanced `i_dlm_dir_evicted_gen` so every subsequent modify fast-pathed (`P106-MR-SKIP`) onto stale cached dir blocks. Evidence: `DIR-STALE-SKIP ino=131 buf_gen=0 inode_gen=365` (block never refreshed across 365 reloads) with all evict probes at zero. Both zsl failure modes — quiet dirent loss (26–70/iter) and the cluster-wide `corrupt dinode 131 (btree extents)` storm (~1590/iter, via stale bmbt children) — are downstream of this one gap.

**Fix (build `FF401F22`, untested):** gate the fences on *extents-loaded* (`xfs_need_iread_extents`) instead of fork format — the iext walk works for BTREE forks too; unenumerable dirs now report not-coherent instead of lying. A first attempt using a per-AG buffer-cache owner-walk was functionally correct but O(whole cache) per modify and starved the dir-EX handoff cluster-wide (`SESS50-STARVE` wedge) — retired.

**Also fixed:** the zsl harness now actually delivers `INSMOD_OPTS` (prep script pre-loads the module param-less; forced fresh load added) — two earlier "instrumented" runs had silently run with the detector disarmed. New `P134-BMBT-WR/REVERT` write-side probe added.

**Next session:** clean the cluster, run one zsl iteration on `FF401F22` with `dirwr=1`; if quiet loss persists, apply the planned destaged-AIL-residue retirement (`xfs_buf_item_done` + delwri-flag clear) to the evict's `undurable` test; the P124 AG-meta stale-push mechanism remains open behind it. Full detail in memory `sess32-run14d-zsl-btree-dir-fence-root`.

